I had a nymph steal 8 potions of holy water and 2 food rations, then 
after a short search and casting of detect monsters, she was nowhere to 
be found on the level.  I cast detect monsters upstairs and downstairs, 
and she wasn't on those levels either, so I figured she'd stepped on a 
known level teleport trap.

Much later, I discovered a pile containing 8 potions of holy water, 2 
food rations, a potion of object detection, and a couple other items.  
There was no corpse, so the nymph is officially listed as "missing, 
presumed dead".  I have my stuff back, but I'm still curious what 
happened to her.

I'm not sure what level I found the pile on relative to where I first 
encountered her, but my leading theory is that she fell down a trap 
door, and was killed by the fall.  I probably got a hit in on her before 
she disappeared.  Is it possible for a monster to die from a fall 
through a trap door?

I'm pretty sure I didn't have a pet at the time, so I don't think a pet 
killed her.  I was wearing conflict on and off, but monsters have to be 
in the line of sight to be affected (I think - CMIIW).  I suppose it's 
possible that I walked into the room and something whacked her in 1 hit 
without my noticing.  There wasn't a monster in the room when I found 
the pile, but I could have passed through the room before.

Any other ideas?

